wayland-scroll-factor (1.0.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Icon: the SVG app icon opened with a comment before the `<svg>`
    tag, and gdk-pixbuf did not recognise it as an image, so GNOME
    menus showed a blank icon (Ubuntu 26.04, Yaru). The comment now
    sits inside the `<svg>` element; the artwork is unchanged. (#45,
    reported by @dradoaica)
  * `scripts/check-icons.sh` loads the app icon the way GNOME does,
    through gdk-pixbuf: the SVG at menu sizes, every PNG at the
    size its folder says, all under the name the desktop file asks
    for. CI runs it on every push, and the distro smoke tests run it
    on the installed icons with each distribution's own gdk-pixbuf,
    so an icon that a menu cannot show never reaches a release again.
  * The Arch smoke lane upgrades the container in full (`pacman -Syu`):
    a plain `-Sy` left Python 3.14.9 next to the image's older glibc,
    and meson could not start.

 -- Daniel Grasso <daniel@the-empty.place>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 00:27:31 +0100

wayland-scroll-factor (1.0.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * `scripts/bump-version.sh` writes a new version into the six files
    that carry one, with the Debian, rpm and AppStream entries generated
    from the CHANGELOG; `scripts/check-version.sh` reads them back,
    in CI on every push and before every publish on a tag.
  * Preload: a factor change is applied from the next scroll or
    pinch event instead of up to 250 ms later. The config directory
    is watched with a non-blocking inotify fd; the 250 ms `stat()`
    stays as the fallback for network homes and for a config directory
    created after login. (#42, by @ritesh-777)

 -- Daniel Grasso <daniel@the-empty.place>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 14:47:29 +0100

